    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/stdio.h.html\">stdio.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nsize_t fread(void *restrict</tt> <i>ptr</i><tt>, size_t</tt> <i>size</i><tt>, size_t</tt> <i>nitems</i><tt>,<br>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; FILE *restrict</tt> <i>stream</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_180_03\" id=\"tag_17_180_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]fread[/I5]() function shall read into the array pointed to by [I6]ptr[/I6] up to [I7]nitems[/I7] elements whose size is\nspecified by [I8]size[/I8] in bytes, from the stream pointed to by [I9]stream[/I9]. For each object, [I10]size[/I10] calls shall be made to\nthe [A11][I12]fgetc[/I12]()[/A11] function and the results stored, in the order read, in an array of\n[B13]unsigned char[/B13] exactly overlaying the object. The file position indicator for the stream (if defined) shall be advanced by\nthe number of bytes successfully read. If an error occurs, the resulting value of the file position indicator for the stream is\nunspecified. If a partial element is read, its value is unspecified.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A11": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fgetc.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B13": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "[S14][[A15]CX[/A15]][/S14] [IMG16] The\n[I17]fread[/I17]() function may mark the last data access timestamp of the file associated with [I18]stream[/I18] for update. The last data\naccess timestamp shall be marked for update by the first successful execution of [A19][I20]fgetc[/I20]()[/A19], [A21][I22]fgets[/I22]()[/A21], [I23]fread[/I23](), [A24][I25]fscanf[/I25]()[/A24], [A26][I27]getc[/I27]()[/A26], [A28][I29]getchar[/I29]()[/A28], [A30][I31]getdelim[/I31]()[/A30], [A32][I33]getline[/I33]()[/A32], or [A34][I35]scanf[/I35]()[/A34] using [I36]stream[/I36] that\nreturns data not supplied by a prior call to [A37][I38]ungetc[/I38]()[/A37]. [IMG39]",
    "placeholders": {
